"inference": {"question": "What is the primary argument against digital restoration?", "correct": "It may alter the intended aesthetic experience by removing original visual characteristics.", "distractors": ["It makes films impossible to view online.", "It takes too much time to perform on older films.", "It increases the cost of film production significantly."], "explanation": "The text notes that digital improvements may strip films of their grain and erase evidence of age/texture."},
"fourth": {"type": "negative", "question": "Which of the following is NOT listed as a concern regarding digital film archiving?", "correct": "Lack of interest from the general public in viewing rare films.", "distractors": ["The potential for data corruption ('bit rot').", "The reliance on proprietary software for access.", "The loss of original aesthetic texture."], "explanation": "The passage discusses archival and accessibility concerns, but does not mention a lack of public interest."}
