"Precession is the slow wobble of Earth's rotational axis, similar to a spinning top slowing down, tracing out a full circle roughly every 26,000 years. Precession alters the orientation of the axis relative to the stars, changing which hemisphere points toward the sun during perihelion (closest approach to the sun). Climate scientists have shown that ice ages are triggered when these three cycles align to produce cool summers in the Northern Hemisphere, preventing winter snow from melting entirely and allowing ice sheets to progressively build up."
